abstract: >-
  LOGACer (Logiciel Online pour la Gestion et l'Analyse de la Céramique)
  was initially developed under the name DBCer as part of the PhD
  dissertation "Étude chronologique, économique et culturelle de la
  vaisselle du Piano della Civita à Artena (Latium) depuis la République
  romaine jusqu’à l’Antiquité tardive" (S. Dienst, 2024).
  Its initial purpose was to structure and share the archaeological data
  produced during this research in a format that could be fully exploited
  by the scientific community, following the principles of Open Science
  and Open Access.

  The classification and sharing of archaeological data represent
  important challenges for archaeological research. LOGACer provides
  tools not only for making such data accessible, but also for comparing
  and combining information produced by different research teams
  collaborating on shared research questions.

  The software is designed to be accessible to researchers wishing to
  manage, analyse and share archaeological data, particularly relating
  to archaeological artefacts, pottery and glassware.